| Method                | Blocks        | Interruptible |
| --------------------- | ------------- | ------------- |
| `lock()`              | Yes           | ❌ No          |
| `lockInterruptibly()` | Yes           | ✅ Yes         |
| `tryLock()`           | No            | ❌ No          |
| `tryLock(timeout)`    | Yes (bounded) | ✅ Yes         |


| Aspect           | `synchronized` | `ReentrantLock`    |
| ---------------- | -------------- | ------------------ |
| Reentrant        | ✅ Yes          | ✅ Yes           |
| Owner tracked    | JVM            | Java object        |
| Hold count       | Hidden         | Visible            |
| Unlocking        | Automatic      | Manual             |
| Mis-unlock risk  | Impossible     | Possible           |
| Condition queues | One (`wait`)   | Many (`Condition`) |
| Fairness         | No             | Optional           |

===========Re-entrant behavior w/Synch ================
synchronized (obj) {
    foo();
}

synchronized (obj) {
    bar();
}
✔ Safe — compiler + JVM guarantee correctness.
==============================

===========Re-entrant behavior lock ================
lock.lock();
foo();
lock.lock();   // reentrant
bar();
lock.unlock(); // count = 1
lock.unlock(); // count = 0 → released
✔ Works — but only if unlock count matches.
❌ Miss one unlock() → permanent lock leak.
========================

====================
ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();

lock.lock();        // holdCount = 1
lock.lock();        // holdCount = 2

System.out.println(lock.getHoldCount()); // 2

lock.unlock();      // holdCount = 1
lock.unlock();      // holdCount = 0 → lock released
=======

================
boolean acquired = lock.tryLock();
try {
    if (!acquired) {
        return;
    }
    process();
} finally {
    if (lock.isHeldByCurrentThread()) {
        lock.unlock();
    }
}
unlock() must be called only by the owning thread
Calling unlock() from a non-owner thread → IllegalMonitorStateException
